        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(qa): repair smoke scenario lane selection",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe channel-sharded QA Smoke experiment in #101164 exposed three failures that were previously hidden behind mixed-channel suite planning:\n\n- `channel-chat-baseline` shared transport state with another Telegram scenario, so its silence assertion observed an unrelated outbound marker.\n- `slack-restart-resume` was selected for Crabline even though Crabline's Slack admin ingress currently records provider state but does not deliver HTTP event callbacks into OpenClaw.\n- `whatsapp-restart-resume` was selected for Crabline even though the WhatsApp channel requires a linked Baileys auth store and Crabline does not seed linked credentials.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n- Mark `channel-chat-baseline` isolated so its silence-sensitive assertion owns a fresh transport and gateway.\n- Mark the Slack and WhatsApp restart-resume scenarios `requiredChannelDriver: live`; they remain covered by their real channel lanes instead of timing out in deterministic Crabline smoke.\n- Add catalog regression assertions for both ownership decisions.\n- Revert #101185 on this branch so exact-head CI attempts QA Smoke and exposes the remaining workflow-level mixed Telegram/Matrix planning gap before the #101164 replacement is prepared.\n\n## User Impact\n\nQA Smoke no longer schedules channel scenarios on deterministic drivers that cannot satisfy their runtime prerequisites, and the Telegram baseline cannot fail from another scenario's outbound traffic. The automatic monolithic job is intentionally re-enabled on this PR for evidence; it is still expected to require the channel-sharded replacement because the valid smoke selection contains both Telegram and Matrix scenarios.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Preserved CI artifacts from run `28820059322`:\n  - Telegram baseline failed after seeing `QA-TELEGRAM-REPLY-CHAIN-OK` from another shared scenario.\n  - Slack recorded admin ingress twice but produced no Slack event callback or outbound delivery.\n  - WhatsApp never reached a running account and timed out twice waiting for transport readiness.\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/qa-lab/src/scenario-catalog.test.ts extensions/qa-lab/src/suite-planning.test.ts test/scripts/ci-workflow-guards.test.ts` — 95 tests passed.\n- Focused local fallback: `channel-chat-baseline` + `telegram-reply-chain-exact-marker` passed together with concurrency 2 after isolation.\n- Static profile check: deterministic smoke now selects 89 scenarios across Telegram and Matrix; Slack and WhatsApp restart scenarios are excluded from Crabline and retained for live lanes.\n- `git diff --check` — passed.\n- Fresh autoreview — clean.\n\nRemote Testbox proof was attempted first but Blacksmith remained queued; the focused Telegram repro used the documented local fallback.\n",
